IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcimr-dates`

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- Part 4 Division 7, noise-induced hearing loss (NIHL):
-- noisy employment (reg 40), the tests and assessment a claim needs (reg 41), who pays for them (regs 43, 44, 48), when an
-- ENT specialist may assess (reg 46), when and from whom I may claim (reg 51), my claim passed to the insurer (regs 53, 54, a
-- regulative rule), the insurer's decision and when liability is taken to be accepted (regs 56, 57), disputes (regs 59,
-- 60), and when I must be paid (reg 61).
--
-- SEAT: the worker with hearing loss. Every question is one the worker asks ("Who pays for my hearing test?", "May I
-- claim?", "By when must I be paid?"). Duties on the employer, the insurer and WorkCover WA are encoded for what they mean
-- to the worker.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING
-- (with a NOTHING-kind comment) where it does not answer.
--
-- Edition: compilation version 00-c0-00, current from 30 June 2026 (mrdoc 49606), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49606.txt (regs 43 and 57 as amended by SL 2024/89 and SL 2026/35).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 19 October 2026, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- noise-induced hearing loss`

§§ `reg 40 -- noisy employment`

-- Reg 40(2): "Employment is noisy employment if, in the course of the employment, a worker is or was frequently required to
-- wear personal protective equipment to reduce the risk of hearing loss associated with noise exposure that exceeds -- (a)
-- an LAeq,8h of 85dB(A); or (b) an LC,peak of 140dB(C)." "Exceeds" is strictly above: 85 dB(A) itself does not.
@export Is my employment noisy employment for hearing loss compensation (reg 40(2))?
GIVEN `I am or was frequently required to wear hearing protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether in this employment you are or were frequently required to wear personal protective equipment to reduce the risk of hearing loss from noise
      `the 8-hour average noise level in dB(A)` IS A NUMBER @desc The 8-hour equivalent continuous A-weighted sound level of the noise the protection was for (LAeq,8h, AS/NZS 1269.1:2005), in dB(A)
      `the peak noise level in dB(C)` IS A NUMBER @desc The C-weighted peak sound level of that noise (LC,peak), in dB(C)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment noisy employment` IF
        `I am or was frequently required to wear hearing protection`
    AND (   `the 8-hour average noise level in dB(A)` GREATER THAN 85
         OR `the peak noise level in dB(C)` GREATER THAN 140)

§§ `regs 43, 44, 48 -- who pays for the hearing test and the assessment`

DECLARE `Who pays for my test` IS ONE OF
    `my current employer`
    `my last noisy employer`
    `I do`
    `not settled by the text: my noisy employer paid for a test less than 2 years ago`

-- Reg 43(1): "The cost of an audiological test must be paid for by -- (a) if the current employer of the worker is a noisy
-- employer -- the current employer of the worker; or (b) if the worker is no longer employed in noisy employment -- the last
-- noisy employer of the worker but only if the worker was employed by that noisy employer within a period of 3 months
-- ending on the day on which the audiological test is performed; or (c) if paragraph (a) or (b) does not apply -- the
-- worker." (2): the cost includes the worker's reasonable expenses. Reg 44: "A noisy employer must pay for a worker's
-- audiological test not more frequently than once every 2 years." Where reg 44 relieves the employer, reg 43(1)(c) does not
-- in terms apply (paragraph (a) or (b) still does), so the text does not say who pays (finding 2; fork F7). The 3 months
-- "ending on" the test day run from the day after the same day 3 months earlier.
GIVEN `my current employer is a noisy employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my last noisy employment ended within the 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer paid for a test less than 2 years ago` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who pays for my test`
`who pays, given` `my current employer is a noisy employer` `and` `my last noisy employment ended within the 3 months` `and` `the employer paid for a test less than 2 years ago` MEANS
    BRANCH IF     (`my current employer is a noisy employer` OR `my last noisy employment ended within the 3 months`)
              AND `the employer paid for a test less than 2 years ago`
           THEN `not settled by the text: my noisy employer paid for a test less than 2 years ago`
           IF `my current employer is a noisy employer` THEN `my current employer`
           IF `my last noisy employment ended within the 3 months` THEN `my last noisy employer`
           OTHERWISE `I do`

GIVEN `the day of the test` IS A DATE
      `my current employer is a noisy employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my last noisy employment ended` IS A DATE
      `that employer paid for an earlier test of mine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of that earlier test` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Who pays for my test`
`who pays for the test on` `the day of the test` `with current noisy employer` `my current employer is a noisy employer` `last noisy employment ending` `the day my last noisy employment ended` `earlier paid test` `that employer paid for an earlier test of mine` `on` `the day of that earlier test` MEANS
    `who pays, given` `my current employer is a noisy employer` `and` `within 3 months` `and` `less than 2 years ago`
    WHERE
        `within 3 months` MEANS
            (NOT `my current employer is a noisy employer`)
            AND `the day my last noisy employment ended` `is on or after` (`the first day of the` 3 `months ending on` `the day of the test`)
        `less than 2 years ago` MEANS
            `that employer paid for an earlier test of mine`
            AND `the day of the test` `is before` (`the date` 2 `years after` `the day of that earlier test`)

@export Who must pay for my hearing (audiological) test (regs 43(1), 44)?
GIVEN `my current employer is a noisy employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your current employer employs you in noisy employment
      `the day my last noisy employment ended` IS A DATE @desc If you are no longer in noisy employment: the last day you were employed by your last noisy employer (any day otherwise)
      `the day of the test` IS A DATE @desc The day the audiological test is or was performed
      `that employer paid for an earlier test of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer who would pay (your current or last noisy employer) has paid for an earlier audiological test of yours
      `the day of that earlier test` IS A DATE @desc The day of that earlier test (any day if none)
GIVETH A `Who pays for my test`
`Who must pay for my hearing test` MEANS
    `who pays for the test on` `the day of the test` `with current noisy employer` `my current employer is a noisy employer` `last noisy employment ending` `the day my last noisy employment ended` `earlier paid test` `that employer paid for an earlier test of mine` `on` `the day of that earlier test`

-- Reg 48(1): "The cost of an NIHL assessment must be paid for by -- (a) the employer required under regulation 43(1)(a) or
-- (b) to pay for the audiological test; or (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply -- the worker." Reg 44 limits only the
-- audiological test, so for the assessment the employer under reg 43(1)(a) or (b) pays even where reg 44 relieved it of
-- the test (fork F7).
@export Who must pay for my NIHL assessment by an ENT specialist (reg 48(1))?
GIVEN `my current employer is a noisy employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your current employer employs you in noisy employment
      `the day my last noisy employment ended` IS A DATE @desc If you are no longer in noisy employment: the last day you were employed by your last noisy employer (any day otherwise)
      `the day of the audiological test` IS A DATE @desc The day of the audiological test the assessment follows
GIVETH A `Who pays for my test`
`Who must pay for my NIHL assessment` MEANS
    `who pays for the test on` `the day of the audiological test` `with current noisy employer` `my current employer is a noisy employer` `last noisy employment ending` `the day my last noisy employment ended` `earlier paid test` FALSE `on` `the day of the audiological test`

-- Reg 43(7): "If the cost of an audiological test is paid for by a worker who subsequently makes a successful claim for
-- noise-induced hearing loss compensation, the last employer liable to deal with the claim and pay compensation must
-- reimburse to the worker the cost of the audiological test." Reg 48(3): the same for the NIHL assessment.
@export Must my last employer pay me back what I paid for my hearing test and NIHL assessment (regs 43(7), 48(3))?
GIVEN `I paid for the audiological test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid for the audiological test yourself
      `what I paid for the test` IS A NUMBER @desc What the test cost you, including expenses reasonably incurred for it, in dollars
      `I paid for the NIHL assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid for the NIHL assessment yourself
      `what I paid for the assessment` IS A NUMBER @desc What the assessment cost you, including any further tests the ENT specialist asked for and your reasonable expenses, in dollars
      `my claim succeeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim for noise-induced hearing loss compensation succeeded
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What must my last employer pay me back` MEANS
    IF `my claim succeeded`
    THEN JUST ((IF `I paid for the audiological test` THEN `what I paid for the test` ELSE 0)
               PLUS (IF `I paid for the NIHL assessment` THEN `what I paid for the assessment` ELSE 0))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: regs 43(7) and 48(3) speak only of a successful claim)

§§ `regs 41, 46, 51 -- may I claim`

-- Reg 40(1): "initial hearing loss means hearing loss suffered by a worker who has not previously received noise-induced
-- hearing loss compensation"; "further hearing loss" is loss in addition to initial loss already compensated.
-- Reg 46: "An ENT specialist may perform an NIHL assessment ... if an audiological test performed in accordance with
-- regulation 45 indicates -- (a) 10% or more initial hearing loss; or (b) 5% or more further hearing loss."
GIVEN `the percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `I have had NIHL compensation before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the percentage` `reaches the threshold, compensated before` `I have had NIHL compensation before` IF
    IF `I have had NIHL compensation before`
    THEN `the percentage` AT LEAST 5
    ELSE `the percentage` AT LEAST 10

@export May an ENT specialist assess my noise-induced hearing loss for a claim (reg 46)?
GIVEN `I have had NIHL compensation before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have previously received noise-induced hearing loss compensation (so this is further hearing loss)
      `the hearing loss my audiological test shows, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of hearing loss your audiological test indicates (initial loss, or the further loss since your last compensation)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an ENT specialist assess my hearing loss` IF
    `the hearing loss my audiological test shows, in per cent` `reaches the threshold, compensated before` `I have had NIHL compensation before`

-- Reg 41: "A claim for noise-induced hearing loss compensation can only be made if a worker has undergone -- (a) an
-- audiological test performed by an authorised audiologist in accordance with Subdivision 2; and (b) an NIHL assessment
-- performed by an ENT specialist in accordance with Subdivision 3." Reg 51(1): "A worker may make a claim ... if an NIHL
-- assessment performed in accordance with regulation 49 indicates -- (a) 10% or more initial NIHL; or (b) 5% or more
-- further NIHL." (5): "The NIHL assessment ... must be performed within the period of 12 months ending on the day on which
-- the claim is made." The 12 months ending on the claim day start the day after the same day a year earlier (fork F1).
@export May I claim compensation for noise-induced hearing loss (regs 41, 51(1), (5))?
GIVEN `an authorised audiologist tested me under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had an audiological test by an audiologist accredited by Audiology Australia (or an approved equivalent body), done to the CEO's standards
      `an ENT specialist assessed me under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had an NIHL assessment by a registered otolaryngologist, done as regulation 49 requires
      `I have had NIHL compensation before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have previously received noise-induced hearing loss compensation (so this is further hearing loss)
      `the hearing loss the NIHL assessment shows, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of noise-induced hearing loss the NIHL assessment indicates
      `the day of the NIHL assessment` IS A DATE @desc The day the ENT specialist performed the NIHL assessment
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you give (or will give) your last employer the claim form and both reports
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I claim NIHL compensation` IF
        `an authorised audiologist tested me under the regulations`
    AND `an ENT specialist assessed me under the regulations`
    AND `the hearing loss the NIHL assessment shows, in per cent` `reaches the threshold, compensated before` `I have had NIHL compensation before`
    AND `the day of the NIHL assessment` `is on or after` (`the first day of the` 12 `months ending on` `the day I make my claim`)
    AND `the day of the NIHL assessment` `is on or before` `the day I make my claim`

-- Reg 51(2): compensation "must be claimed from the employer (the last employer) who last employed the worker in employment
-- of a nature to which the NIHL assessment report indicates the noise-induced hearing loss is or was due." (3): "If the
-- worker is or was working concurrently for 2 or more employers in employment of a nature referred to in subregulation
-- (2), the employer for whom the worker worked the longest is the last employer." An arbitrator may later find another
-- employer is the last employer (regs 59(4)(c), 60(3)(c)).
@export Is this employer the last employer I must claim my hearing loss compensation from (reg 51(2), (3))?
GIVEN `it last employed me in the kind of work my NIHL report blames` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this employer is the one who last employed you in employment of the kind the NIHL assessment report says caused your hearing loss
      `I worked for 2 or more such employers at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at the end you were working concurrently for 2 or more employers in that kind of employment
      `I worked longest for this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether this is the employer you worked for the longest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this employer my last employer` IF
    IF `I worked for 2 or more such employers at the same time`
    THEN `I worked longest for this one`
    ELSE `it last employed me in the kind of work my NIHL report blames`

-- Reg 51(4): "A claim for noise-induced hearing loss compensation is made when a worker has given to the last employer --
-- (a) a completed claim form in the approved form; and (b) the worker's audiological test report; and (c) the worker's NIHL
-- assessment report."
@export Have I made my claim for noise-induced hearing loss compensation (reg 51(4))?
GIVEN `I gave my last employer the completed claim form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your last employer a completed claim form in the approved form
      `I gave it my audiological test report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given it your audiological test report
      `I gave it my NIHL assessment report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given it your NIHL assessment report
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I made my NIHL claim` IF
        `I gave my last employer the completed claim form`
    AND `I gave it my audiological test report`
    AND `I gave it my NIHL assessment report`

§§ `regs 53, 54 -- my claim passed to the insurer`

DECLARE `Hearing party` IS ONE OF
    `my last employer`

DECLARE `Hearing act` IS ONE OF
    `give my claim to its insurer`

-- Reg 53(1): "An insured last employer must, within 7 days after a worker claims noise-induced hearing loss compensation
-- from the last employer in accordance with regulation 51, give the worker's claim to the insurer. Penalty ... a fine of
-- $5 000." Time 0 is the day I claimed; the last day is day 7.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Hearing party` `Hearing act`
`reg 53 -- my insured last employer must give my claim to its insurer within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `my last employer`
    MUST `give my claim to its insurer`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST BREACH BY `my last employer` BECAUSE "the claim was not given to the insurer within 7 days after it was made (reg 53(1))"

-- Reg 54(1): "If an insured last employer from which a worker has claimed noise-induced hearing loss compensation fails to
-- give the claim to the insurer in accordance with regulation 53, the worker may give the claim to the insurer." (3): a
-- claim the worker gives "is taken to have been given to the insurer by the last employer". A self-insured last employer
-- has no insurer and reg 54 does not speak to it: NOTHING. While the 7 days run, or once the employer has passed the claim
-- on in time, the "if" is not met: JUST FALSE.
@export May I give my hearing loss claim to my employer's insurer myself (regs 53, 54)?
GIVEN `my last employer is insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your last employer is insured under a workers compensation policy (rather than self-insured)
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave your last employer the claim form and both reports
      `my employer has given my claim to its insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has given your claim to its insurer
      `the day it did` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I give my NIHL claim to the insurer myself` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my last employer is insured`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit: reg 54 speaks only of an insured last employer)
    ELSE IF `my employer has given my claim to its insurer`
         THEN `the answer for` (EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`day` `the day it did`)), (EVENT `my last employer` `give my claim to its insurer` (`day` `the day it did`))))
         ELSE `the answer for` (EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`day` `today`)), (EVENT `my last employer` `give my claim to its insurer` (`day` `today`))))
    WHERE
        `the rule` MEANS `reg 53 -- my insured last employer must give my claim to its insurer within 7 days`
        GIVEN `a day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `day` `a day` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the day I made my claim` `to` `a day`)
        GIVEN `the outcome` IS A DEONTIC `Hearing party` `Hearing act`
        GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `the answer for` `the outcome` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the outcome`
            WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `regs 56, 57 -- the insurer's decision on my hearing loss claim`

-- Reg 56(1): "Within 14 days after a claim is given to an insurer or self-insurer, the insurer or self-insurer must give a
-- noise-induced hearing loss liability decision notice ... to ... (a) the worker". (3): instead, within the same 14 days, an
-- NIHL deferred decision notice. (5): "If an insurer or self-insurer fails to give an NIHL liability decision notice or NIHL
-- deferred decision notice as and when required by this regulation, the insurer or self-insurer is taken to have accepted
-- that the last employer is liable to pay the worker noise-induced hearing loss compensation." (6)(a): a claim on a
-- self-insured last employer "is considered to have been given to the self-insurer when it is made by the worker".
-- Reg 57(1): after a deferred notice, the liability decision notice must come "before the day after the period of 120 days
-- beginning on the day on which the insurer or self-insurer receives a claim", that is by day 119 counting the day of
-- receipt as day 0 (fork F1); (3): if not, liability is "taken to have [been] accepted".
@export By when must the insurer give me its decision on liability for my hearing loss claim (regs 56(1), (3), 57(1))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was given my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was given to the insurer (for a self-insured employer, the day you made the claim)
      `the insurer gave me a deferred decision notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer gave you an NIHL deferred decision notice within 14 days after it was given the claim
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the insurer decide my NIHL claim` MEANS
    IF `the insurer gave me a deferred decision notice in time`
    THEN `the date` 119 `days after` `the day the insurer was given my claim`
    ELSE `the date` 14 `days after` `the day the insurer was given my claim`

@export Is my last employer taken to have accepted liability for my hearing loss claim because the insurer did not decide in time (regs 56(5), 57(3))?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was given my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was given to the insurer (for a self-insured employer, the day you made the claim)
      `the insurer gave me a liability decision notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you an NIHL liability decision notice (accepting liability or not)
      `the day of the liability decision notice` IS A DATE @desc The day it gave you that notice (any day if not)
      `the insurer gave me a deferred decision notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer gave you an NIHL deferred decision notice
      `the day of the deferred decision notice` IS A DATE @desc The day it gave you that notice (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is liability for my NIHL claim taken to be accepted` IF
    IF `a decision came within 14 days`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `a deferral came within 14 days`
         THEN IF `the insurer gave me a liability decision notice`
              THEN `the day of the liability decision notice` `is after` (`the date` 119 `days after` `the day the insurer was given my claim`)
              ELSE `today` `is after` (`the date` 119 `days after` `the day the insurer was given my claim`)
         ELSE `today` `is after` `the 14th day`
    WHERE
        `the 14th day` MEANS `the date` 14 `days after` `the day the insurer was given my claim`
        `a decision came within 14 days` MEANS
            `the insurer gave me a liability decision notice`
            AND `the day of the liability decision notice` `is on or before` `the 14th day`
        `a deferral came within 14 days` MEANS
            `the insurer gave me a deferred decision notice`
            AND `the day of the deferred decision notice` `is on or before` `the 14th day`
        GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `the first day` `is after` `the second day` MEANS `the second day` `is before` `the first day`

§§ `regs 59, 60 -- disputes`

DECLARE `The insurer's answer` IS ONE OF
    `liability accepted`
    `not accepted: I am not a worker`
    `not accepted: my hearing loss is below the threshold`
    `not accepted: this employer is not my last employer`
    `not accepted: hearing loss matters are disputed`

-- Reg 60(1): "If a liability decision notice ... states that liability is not accepted on the basis of 1 or more of the
-- matters set out in regulation 56(2)(b)(i) to (iii), a worker may apply under Part 6 of the Act for determination of the
-- dispute." Reg 59(1): where it is not accepted because hearing loss matters are disputed under s 113, "the insurer or
-- self-insurer must apply"; (2): "If a worker disputes 1 or more hearing loss matters under section 113 of the Act, the
-- worker may apply"; (3): with a copy of an NIHL assessment report. Otherwise the regulations give the worker no
-- application of their own: NOTHING.
@export May I apply to an arbitrator to decide my hearing loss dispute (regs 59, 60)?
GIVEN `the insurer's answer` IS A `The insurer's answer` @desc What the insurer's NIHL liability decision notice says
      `I dispute a hearing loss matter under s 113` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you dispute one or more hearing loss matters under section 113 of the Act (for example the percentage of loss)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I apply to an arbitrator about my NIHL claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the insurer's answer`
    WHEN `not accepted: I am not a worker` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `not accepted: my hearing loss is below the threshold` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `not accepted: this employer is not my last employer` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `I dispute a hearing loss matter under s 113`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: regs 59 and 60 give no other application by the worker)

§§ `reg 61 -- when I must be paid`

-- Reg 61: "The last employer must pay the worker noise-induced hearing loss compensation and, if required, the costs of the
-- audiological test and NIHL assessment -- (a) within 14 days after -- (i) the worker is given an NIHL liability decision
-- notice that states the insurer or self-insurer accepts that the last employer is liable ...; or (ii) an arbitrator
-- determines, under regulation 59 or 60, which employer is liable as the last employer ...; or (b) if another law
-- (including a Commonwealth law) prevents payment within the period provided for in paragraph (a) -- within 7 days after
-- payment is permitted under that other law."
@export By when must my last employer pay my hearing loss compensation (reg 61)?
GIVEN `the day liability was accepted or determined` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the NIHL liability decision notice accepting liability, or the day an arbitrator determined which employer is liable as the last employer
      `another law prevents payment in that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another law (including a Commonwealth law) prevents payment within 14 days after that day
      `the day payment is permitted under that law` IS A DATE @desc The day that other law permits payment (any day if not)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I be paid my NIHL compensation` MEANS
    IF `another law prevents payment in that time`
    THEN `the date` 7 `days after` `the day payment is permitted under that law`
    ELSE `the date` 14 `days after` `the day liability was accepted or determined`
